From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Generate err_data.c without Go module mode

err_data_generate.go imports nothing but the standard library, but `go run`
resolves go.mod first, and go.mod requires golang.org/x/crypto and
golang.org/x/net for the test tooling. So generating one C file reaches for the
module proxy and the build fails without network:

    go: golang.org/x/crypto@v0.0.0-20210513164829-c07d793c2f9a:
        dial tcp: lookup proxy.golang.org: network is unreachable

GO111MODULE=off skips go.mod entirely, which is correct for a file that needs
none of it.

Only this call site: the others run test and fuzzer tooling that is not built
here, and would need the modules if it were.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [applies to a vendored dependency of firebase-cpp-sdk]
Signed-off-by: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
---
--- a/crypto/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/crypto/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -169,7 +169,8 @@
 
 add_custom_command(
   OUTPUT err_data.c
-  COMMAND ${GO_EXECUTABLE} run err_data_generate.go > ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/err_data.c
+  COMMAND ${CMAKE_COMMAND} -E env GO111MODULE=off
+          ${GO_EXECUTABLE} run err_data_generate.go > ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/err_data.c
   DEPENDS
   err/err_data_generate.go
   err/asn1.errordata
